{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Go, ascend from here.</b> He used the language of ascent — perhaps to allude to what they of blessed memory said (Shabbat 88a), that the crowns which Israel had received and then lost, Moses took. And that is the ascent alluded to in His saying <b>ascend from here</b>, meaning from this which has passed. And therefore he was precise also in saying the word <b>you</b>, which there was no need to say since He was speaking with him, but rather to say: you will ascend and no one else — for on the contrary, it was a descent for them. And His saying <b>and the people</b> means: they shall go with you." "<b>Saying.</b> The reason He said <b>saying</b> is that this expression in the words of HaShem was not identical for all of them. Some of them He addressed in this expression, and some of the patriarchs He addressed in a different expression, as is clear from the verses. Therefore He said <b>saying</b> — meaning that the intent of the utterance for all of them is ״to your seed״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:17.891866477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}